/-!
# The level-one modular group as a cofinite Fuchsian group

The effective group acting on the upper half-plane at level one is the image of
`PSL(2, ℤ)` in `PSL(2, ℝ)`, not `SL(2, ℤ)`: the latter still contains the central matrix
`-I`, which acts trivially. This file proves that the projective image is a discrete cofinite
subgroup of `PSL(2, ℝ)`.

The standard open modular fundamental domain is transported from the `PSL(2, ℤ)` action to
its image in `PSL(2, ℝ)`. Its finite hyperbolic area then proves cofiniteness. This supplies the
effective level-one input for quotient and compactification constructions.

The elliptic data of the effective group are transported from `PSL(2, ℤ)` in the same way: the
stabilizers of `i` and `ρ` have orders `2` and `3`, and every point outside their two orbits has
trivial stabilizer. So the free locus of the level-one quotient is the complement of exactly two
orbits.

For a subgroup `Γ ≤ SL(2, ℤ)`, the effective image `Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R` lies in the effective
level-one group, so its point stabilizers are subgroups of the level-one ones: every point with
nontrivial stabilizer in the effective image of `Γ` lies in the `SL(2, ℤ)`-orbit of `i` or of
`ρ`, and that stabilizer has order dividing `2` or `3`. At the translate `γ • i`, the stabilizer
in the effective level-one group is generated by the image of the conjugate `γ S γ⁻¹`. So the
stabilizer in the effective image of `Γ` has order `2` if `γ S γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ` and is trivial
otherwise. At `γ • ρ` the same holds with order `3` for the conjugate of the order-three matrix
`T⁻¹ S`: the other noncentral matrices of `SL(2, ℤ)` fixing `ρ` are `± S T` and `-T⁻¹ S`, and
each has `T⁻¹ S` as a power. These criteria turn the elliptic-point counts of a congruence
subgroup into congruence conditions on the bottom row of `γ`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.ModularGroup.isFundamentalDomain_fdo_psl2zToPSL2RRange`: the standard open modular
  domain is a fundamental domain for the projective image in `PSL(2, ℝ)`.
* `TauCeti.ModularGroup.isCofinite_psl2zToPSL2RRange`: that image is a cofinite Fuchsian group.
* `TauCeti.ModularGroup.card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_I` and
  `TauCeti.ModularGroup.card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_ρ`: the elliptic orders `2` and `3`.
* `TauCeti.ModularGroup.quotientMk_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_iff_quotientMk_sl_eq`: the orbits of the
  projective image are those of `SL(2, ℤ)`.
* `TauCeti.ModularGroup.stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_bot_iff`: a stabilizer is trivial exactly
  off the orbits of `i` and `ρ`.
* `Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_smul_I` and `Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_smul_ρ`: the stabilizer
  orders in the effective image of `Γ` at `γ • i` and at `γ • ρ`.
* `Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_eq_one_of_orbit_ne`: off the orbits of `i` and `ρ` the stabilizer
  in the effective image of `Γ` is trivial.
* `Subgroup.exists_smul_eq_of_card_stabilizer_ne_one`: a point with nontrivial stabilizer in the
  effective image of `Γ` is a translate of `i` or `ρ`, with stabilizer order `2` or `3`.

## References

* Fred Diamond and Jerry Shurman, *A First Course in Modular Forms*, Graduate Texts in
  Mathematics 228, Springer, 2005, §§2.3–2.4.
* Jean-Pierre Serre, *A Course in Arithmetic*, Graduate Texts in Mathematics 7, Springer,
  1973, Chapter VII.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory MulAction UpperHalfPlane

open scoped MatrixGroups

namespace TauCeti.ModularGroup

/-- The standard open modular domain is a fundamental domain for the image of `PSL(2, ℤ)` in
`PSL(2, ℝ)`. It presents the effective level-one quotient and supplies the finite-area domain
used to prove that the projective image is cofinite. -/
theorem isFundamentalDomain_fdo_psl2zToPSL2RRange :
    IsFundamentalDomain psl2zToPSL2R.range (_root_.ModularGroup.fdo : Set ℍ) volume := by
  simpa only [Set.preimage_id] using
    _root_.ModularGroup.isFundamentalDomain_fdo.preimage_of_equiv
      (QuasiMeasurePreserving.id volume)
      (MonoidHom.ofInjective psl2zToPSL2R_injective).bijective
      fun g τ ↦ by
        simp only [id_eq, MonoidHom.ofInjective_apply, Subgroup.smul_def,
          UpperHalfPlane.psl2zToPSL2R_smul]

/-- The image of `PSL(2, ℤ)` in `PSL(2, ℝ)` is a cofinite Fuchsian group. -/
theorem isCofinite_psl2zToPSL2RRange : psl2zToPSL2R.range.IsCofinite := by
  apply isFundamentalDomain_fdo_psl2zToPSL2RRange.isCofinite_of_volume_ne_top
  exact ne_of_lt <| by
    rw [← measure_congr _root_.ModularGroup.fd_ae_eq_fdo]
    exact _root_.ModularGroup.volume_fd_lt_top

/-! ### Elliptic points -/

/-- The point stabilizers of the effective level-one group are those of `PSL(2, ℤ)`, transported
along the injective homomorphism `psl2zToPSL2R`. -/
theorem card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl (z : ℍ) :
    Nat.card (stabilizer psl2zToPSL2R.range z) = Nat.card (stabilizer PSL(2, ℤ) z) :=
  TauCeti.card_stabilizer_congr (f := id) (MonoidHom.ofInjective psl2zToPSL2R_injective) z
    (fun g ↦ by
      simp only [id_eq, Subgroup.smul_def, MonoidHom.ofInjective_apply, psl2zToPSL2R_smul])
    fun _ ↦ by simp only [id_eq, imp_self]

/-- Two points lie in the same orbit of the effective level-one group exactly when they lie in
the same orbit of `SL(2, ℤ)`. -/
theorem orbitRel_psl2zToPSL2RRange_iff_orbitRel_sl {z w : ℍ} :
    orbitRel psl2zToPSL2R.range ℍ z w ↔ orbitRel SL(2, ℤ) ℍ z w := by
  simp only [orbitRel_apply, mem_orbit_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨⟨_, p, rfl⟩, h⟩
    induction p using QuotientGroup.induction_on with
    | H a =>
      exact ⟨a, by simpa [Subgroup.smul_def, UpperHalfPlane.psl2zToPSL2R_smul] using h⟩
  · rintro ⟨a, h⟩
    exact ⟨⟨psl2zToPSL2R (a : PSL(2, ℤ)), a, rfl⟩,
      by simpa [Subgroup.smul_def, UpperHalfPlane.psl2zToPSL2R_smul] using h⟩

/-- The stabilizer of `i` in the effective level-one group has order `2`. -/
theorem card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_I :
    Nat.card (stabilizer psl2zToPSL2R.range I) = 2 := by
  rw [card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl, card_stabilizer_psl_I]

/-- The stabilizer of `ρ` in the effective level-one group has order `3`. -/
theorem card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_ρ :
    Nat.card (stabilizer psl2zToPSL2R.range ρ) = 3 := by
  rw [card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl, card_stabilizer_psl_ρ]

/-- Two points have the same orbit under the effective level-one group exactly when they have the
same orbit under `SL(2, ℤ)`. -/
theorem quotientMk_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_iff_quotientMk_sl_eq {z w : ℍ} :
    Quotient.mk (orbitRel psl2zToPSL2R.range ℍ) z = Quotient.mk _ w ↔
      (Quotient.mk'' z : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) = Quotient.mk'' w := by
  rw [Quotient.eq, Quotient.eq'', orbitRel_psl2zToPSL2RRange_iff_orbitRel_sl]

/-- **The elliptic points of the level-one group.** The stabilizer of `z` in the effective
level-one group is trivial exactly when `z` lies in neither the orbit of `i` nor that of `ρ`. -/
theorem stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_bot_iff (z : ℍ) :
    stabilizer psl2zToPSL2R.range z = ⊥ ↔
      Quotient.mk (orbitRel psl2zToPSL2R.range ℍ) z ≠ Quotient.mk _ I ∧
        Quotient.mk (orbitRel psl2zToPSL2R.range ℍ) z ≠ Quotient.mk _ ρ := by
  rw [← Subgroup.card_eq_one, card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl,
    ← ellipticOrder_mk, ne_eq, ne_eq, quotientMk_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_iff_quotientMk_sl_eq,
    quotientMk_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_iff_quotientMk_sl_eq]
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨fun hI ↦ ?_, fun hρ ↦ ?_⟩,
    fun h ↦ ellipticOrder_eq_one_of_orbit_ne_I_of_orbit_ne_ρ h.1 h.2⟩
  · rw [hI, ellipticOrder_I] at h
    omega
  · rw [hρ, ellipticOrder_ρ] at h
    omega

end TauCeti.ModularGroup

/-! ### Elliptic points of subgroups -/

open Matrix Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup ModularGroup TauCeti.ModularGroup

namespace TauCeti

variable (Γ : Subgroup SL(2, ℤ))

open scoped Classical in
/-- **Elliptic stabilizers in `Γ` through a generating conjugate.** Let `z₀` have level-one
elliptic order a prime `p`, and let `E` be a noncentral matrix fixing `z₀` which is a power of
every noncentral matrix fixing `z₀`. Then the stabilizer of `γ • z₀` in the effective image of
`Γ` has order `p` when `γ E γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ`, and is trivial otherwise. -/
private theorem card_stabilizer_map_smul_of_zpow {z₀ : ℍ} {E : SL(2, ℤ)} {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime)
    (horder : ellipticOrder (Quotient.mk'' z₀) = p) (hE : E • z₀ = z₀)
    (hEc : E ∉ Subgroup.center SL(2, ℤ))
    (hgen : ∀ s : SL(2, ℤ), s • z₀ = z₀ → s ∉ Subgroup.center SL(2, ℤ) → ∃ k : ℤ, s ^ k = E)
    (γ : SL(2, ℤ)) :
    Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) (γ • z₀)) = if γ * E * γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ then p else 1 := by
  have hmk : (Quotient.mk'' (γ • z₀) : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) = Quotient.mk'' z₀ :=
    Quotient.sound' ⟨γ, rfl⟩
  have hR : Nat.card (stabilizer psl2zToPSL2R.range (γ • z₀)) = p := by
    rw [card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl, ← ellipticOrder_mk, hmk, horder]
  have hdvd := Subgroup.card_stabilizer_dvd_card_stabilizer
    Γ.map_sl2zToPSL2R_le_range_psl2zToPSL2R (γ • z₀)
  rw [hR] at hdvd
  have hN : (Subgroup.center SL(2, ℤ)).Normal := inferInstance
  -- the stabilizer is nontrivial exactly when the generating conjugate lies in `Γ`
  have hne : stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) (γ • z₀) ≠ ⊥ ↔ γ * E * γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ := by
    constructor
    · intro h
      obtain ⟨⟨⟨_, h', hhΓ, rfl⟩, hfix⟩, hne1⟩ := (Subgroup.ne_bot_iff_exists_ne_one).mp h
      rw [mem_stabilizer_iff, Subgroup.smul_def, sl2zToPSL2R_smul] at hfix
      have hconj : γ * (γ⁻¹ * h' * γ) * γ⁻¹ = h' := by group
      have hs : (γ⁻¹ * h' * γ) • z₀ = z₀ := by
        rw [mul_smul, mul_smul, hfix, inv_smul_smul]
      have hsc : γ⁻¹ * h' * γ ∉ Subgroup.center SL(2, ℤ) := by
        intro hc
        have hc' := hN.conj_mem _ hc γ
        rw [hconj, ← sl2zToPSL2R_ker, MonoidHom.mem_ker] at hc'
        exact hne1 (Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext hc'))
      obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hgen _ hs hsc
      rw [← hk, ← conj_zpow, hconj]
      exact zpow_mem hhΓ k
    · intro h
      refine (Subgroup.ne_bot_iff_exists_ne_one).mpr
        ⟨⟨⟨sl2zToPSL2R (γ * E * γ⁻¹), Subgroup.mem_map_of_mem _ h⟩, ?_⟩, fun h1 ↦ hEc ?_⟩
      · rw [mem_stabilizer_iff, Subgroup.smul_def, sl2zToPSL2R_smul, mul_smul, mul_smul,
          inv_smul_smul, hE]
      · have hmem : γ * E * γ⁻¹ ∈ Subgroup.center SL(2, ℤ) := by
          rw [← sl2zToPSL2R_ker, MonoidHom.mem_ker]
          exact congrArg (fun x ↦ x.1.1) h1
        simpa [mul_assoc] using hN.conj_mem' _ hmem γ
  split_ifs with h
  · rcases hp.eq_one_or_self_of_dvd _ hdvd with h1 | hp'
    · exact absurd (Subgroup.card_eq_one.mp h1) (hne.mpr h)
    · exact hp'
  · exact Subgroup.card_eq_one.mpr (not_not.mp (mt hne.mp h))

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The elliptic points of order two.** The stabilizer of `γ • i` in the effective image of `Γ`
has order `2` when `γ S γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ`, and is trivial otherwise. -/
theorem _root_.Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_smul_I (γ : SL(2, ℤ)) :
    Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) (γ • I)) = if γ * S * γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ then 2 else 1 := by
  refine card_stabilizer_map_smul_of_zpow Γ Nat.prime_two ellipticOrder_I
    (stabilizer_I.mpr (by simp)) ?_ ?_ γ
  · rw [mem_center_iff_eq_one_or_eq_neg_one]
    decide
  · intro s hs hsc
    rw [mem_center_iff_eq_one_or_eq_neg_one] at hsc
    have hmem := stabilizer_I.mp hs
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hmem
    rcases hmem with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact absurd (Or.inl rfl) hsc
    · exact absurd (Or.inr rfl) hsc
    · exact ⟨1, zpow_one S⟩
    · exact ⟨-1, by decide⟩

open scoped Classical in
/-- **The elliptic points of order three.** The stabilizer of `γ • ρ` in the effective image of
`Γ` has order `3` when `γ (T⁻¹ S) γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ`, and is trivial otherwise. -/
theorem _root_.Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_smul_ρ (γ : SL(2, ℤ)) :
    Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) (γ • ρ)) =
      if γ * (T⁻¹ * S) * γ⁻¹ ∈ Γ then 3 else 1 := by
  refine card_stabilizer_map_smul_of_zpow Γ Nat.prime_three ellipticOrder_ρ
    (stabilizer_ρ.mpr (by simp)) ?_ ?_ γ
  · rw [mem_center_iff_eq_one_or_eq_neg_one]
    decide
  · intro s hs hsc
    rw [mem_center_iff_eq_one_or_eq_neg_one] at hsc
    have hmem := stabilizer_ρ.mp hs
    simp only [Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton] at hmem
    rcases hmem with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl
    · exact absurd (Or.inl rfl) hsc
    · exact absurd (Or.inr rfl) hsc
    · exact ⟨2, by decide⟩
    · exact ⟨2, by decide⟩
    · exact ⟨1, zpow_one _⟩
    · exact ⟨4, by decide⟩

/-- **Off the two elliptic orbits the stabilizer is trivial**: a point of `ℍ` outside the
`SL(2, ℤ)`-orbits of `i` and `ρ` has trivial stabilizer in the effective image of `Γ`. -/
theorem _root_.Subgroup.card_stabilizer_map_eq_one_of_orbit_ne {z : ℍ}
    (hI : (Quotient.mk'' z : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) ≠ Quotient.mk'' I)
    (hρ : (Quotient.mk'' z : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) ≠ Quotient.mk'' ρ) :
    Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) z) = 1 := by
  have hdvd := Subgroup.card_stabilizer_dvd_card_stabilizer
    Γ.map_sl2zToPSL2R_le_range_psl2zToPSL2R z
  rwa [card_stabilizer_psl2zToPSL2RRange_eq_card_stabilizer_psl, ← ellipticOrder_mk,
    ellipticOrder_eq_one_of_orbit_ne_I_of_orbit_ne_ρ hI hρ, Nat.dvd_one] at hdvd

/-- **Classification of the elliptic points of `Γ`**: a point with nontrivial stabilizer in the
effective image of `Γ` lies in the `SL(2, ℤ)`-orbit of `i` or of `ρ`, with stabilizer order `2`
or `3` respectively. -/
theorem _root_.Subgroup.exists_smul_eq_of_card_stabilizer_ne_one {z : ℍ}
    (hz : Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) z) ≠ 1) :
    (∃ γ : SL(2, ℤ), γ • I = z ∧ Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) z) = 2) ∨
      ∃ γ : SL(2, ℤ), γ • ρ = z ∧ Nat.card (stabilizer (Γ.map sl2zToPSL2R) z) = 3 := by
  classical
  by_cases hI : (Quotient.mk'' z : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) = Quotient.mk'' I
  · obtain ⟨γ, rfl⟩ := mem_orbit_iff.mp (Quotient.exact' hI)
    rw [Γ.card_stabilizer_map_smul_I] at hz ⊢
    split_ifs at hz ⊢
    exacts [Or.inl ⟨γ, rfl, rfl⟩, absurd rfl hz]
  by_cases hρ : (Quotient.mk'' z : orbitRel.Quotient SL(2, ℤ) ℍ) = Quotient.mk'' ρ
  · obtain ⟨γ, rfl⟩ := mem_orbit_iff.mp (Quotient.exact' hρ)
    rw [Γ.card_stabilizer_map_smul_ρ] at hz ⊢
    split_ifs at hz ⊢
    exacts [Or.inr ⟨γ, rfl, rfl⟩, absurd rfl hz]
  exact absurd (Γ.card_stabilizer_map_eq_one_of_orbit_ne hI hρ) hz

end TauCeti
